  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/common/Relator">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A relator is a reified relation: e.g. parthood reifying the whole-part relation, or meeting reifying the meets relation. Consists of static parts only, which are the roles played by each relata in the relation (with min 2 for a binary relation). A relator is thus specifically (statically) dependent on each role / part (min 2) and on each relata (min 2). Relators can also have qualities, which are also not parts, such as the intensity of the relation.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Relator </rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/common/Nonphysical_Endurant"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nd61eda891d324cf2b12b4208980eba67b154"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nd61eda891d324cf2b12b4208980eba67b155"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nd61eda891d324cf2b12b4208980eba67b156"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nd61eda891d324cf2b12b4208980eba67b157"/>
  </rdf:Description>
