  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/granularmaterial/Pyroclastic_Particle_Material">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Particles ejected during a volcanic eruption. (Jackson, 1997, p. 521). Clast whose origin is a direct result of volcanic process (excludes fragments in lava autobreccia) and has not been reworked by sedimentary processes (Gillespie and Styles 1999). Pyroclasts.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Use for description of pyroclastic rocks</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Pyroclastic particle material</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/granularmaterial/Granular_Particle_Material"/>
  </rdf:Description>
