  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/common/Quality">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A colour, mass, density, etc., that inheres in its bearer. Must have some quality values, and only quality values, as persistent parts, e.g. red or 2.0. These values can change over time, but can't be missing (i.e. a quality must a value to exist and retain identity). This means qualities cannot pause their existence: once they carry no value they cease to exist and cannot exist again, and if a similar quality resurfaces, it would be a different quality. For example, a sponge might have alternating qualities of softness (when wet) and hardness (when dry), with each  being a distinct quality. Qualities can only have values as parts, not other things, but they can possess qualities, such as colour having the qualities hue, value, situation.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Quality</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/gso/1.0/common/Inherant"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nd61eda891d324cf2b12b4208980eba67b139"/>
